  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1123 PM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nPresent model agreement continues to trend towards a decent ridge\nholding over the Panhandles for the majority of Friday, which will\nallow us another dry day. Moving into Saturday, however, does have\nmodels seeing our next chance at active weather come in the form\nof trough moving across the Southwestern United States. At this\ntime present ensembles have been gaining confidence in this trough\nleading to precipitation for the Panhandles with present NBM\ngiving widespread chances around a 40 to 70 percent come Saturday\nafternoon. Still there is a lot of uncertainty present for amounts\nand actual duration of the event, with some of the recent runs of\nthe GFS and ECMWF suggesting chances could linger clear into\nMonday morning. What makes this interesting, is that these same\nmodel have also suggested temperatures in our far northwest could\nbe cold enough that precipitation could transition to snow during\nthe overnight should it still be occurring there. However,\nconfidence in this remains quite low as present ensembles have\nbeen keeping any chances much further east by this time frame.\nRegardless hints of more chances do look to follow next Tuesday,\nthough chance are only around 10 to 20 percent at this time.\nOtherwise, look for temperature to cool with this incoming\nactivity with afternoon highs holding in the 50s to mid 60s.",
